                "senderName": "NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 5 at 9:49PM MDT until September 7 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of Utah, including the following areas, Central\nMountains, Eastern Juab/Millard Counties, Sanpete Valley, Sevier\nValley, Wasatch Plateau/Book Cliffs, Western Uinta Basin, Bryce\nCanyon Country, South Central Utah, Southern Mountains, Upper\nSevier River Valleys, Southwest Utah and Zion National Park. This\nwatch also includes recent burn scars such as Cottonwood, Widemouth\n2, Forsyth, France Canyon, Monroe Canyon, and Black Canyon.\n\n* WHEN...From 9 AM MDT Sunday through Sunday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, dry washes, slot canyons, and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations such as slickrock areas and recent burn\nscars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Excessive rainfall is expected Sunday afternoon associated with\nthe arrival of deep tropical moisture across much of central and\nsouthern Utah. Rates from 0.4-0.6 inches per hour are expected,\nwith isolated higher rates from 0.6-1.0 inches per hour possible.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
