                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 5 at 3:44PM HST until September 8 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "Moisture along the eastern flank of Hurricane Lowell will bring\nperiods of heavy rain to the main Hawaiian Islands late Sunday\nthrough Tuesday.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...All main Hawaiian Islands.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday evening through Tuesday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flood prone roads and other low lying areas may be closed\ndue to elevated runoff and overflowing streams. Urban areas may\nreceive more significant flooding and property damage due to rapid\nrunoff.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Moisture along the eastern flank of Hurricane Lowell will bring\nperiods of heavy rain to the main Hawaiian islands late Sunday\nthrough Tuesday. Initially, the threat of heavy rain will be\nhighest along windward and mountain areas, then the threat will\nspread everywhere as the winds become more southerly by Monday.\n- The entire state.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
